#+TITLE: ALFE must supply a missing Windows USERPROFILE to CAD child processes
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS:

* Symptom and reproduction
An SSH Windows session may have no USERPROFILE even though Windows has a
valid profile for the account. Launching AutoCAD under EPURE in that
environment can fail before READY. The captured startup dump identifies
SNCFOutilsARX64.arx+0x10379, C0000409, fast-fail parameter 2.

Off-host analysis establishes that the vendor routine checks the DWORD
GetEnvironmentVariableW result only for a negative value, then appends
ntuser.dat to an uninitialized stack buffer when the result is zero.
See ../open/alfe-autocad-sncf-arx-startup-failure.issue for the vendor defect.

* Required ALFE behavior
On native Windows, supply a missing or empty inherited USERPROFILE when
launching child processes. Resolve the actual account profile with
SHGetKnownFolderPath(FOLDERID_Profile); do not guess from HOME or an MSYS
home. Preserve a nonempty inherited value and explicit launch overrides.
Fail bootstrap clearly if the Windows profile cannot be resolved.
Scope the repair to the launch and restore the parent's environment.
Do not modify registry, account settings or proprietary binaries.

* Resolved on the unmerged qualification branches, 2026-11-03
Implemented in the shared backend-cad-common.lisp launcher in !507
(commit 27d25b80, version 2.3.94) and !476 (commit 193a844e, version 2.3.97).
Both program versions remain aligned. This issue records the ALFE safeguard,
not a claim that the vendor ARX or the separate shutdown crash is fixed.

Native Windows regressions cover overrides, absent/empty inherited values,
resolution failure, known-folder resolution without USERPROFILE, a real
cscript child's environment and restoration of the parent. Compilation and
loading of the native FASL were verified as well.
Final source heads db2d7ca2 (!507) and e85db5ab (!476) pass their Windows ALFE
unit lanes (jobs 17694845084 and 17694882856). The !507 suite reports 2481
checks and zero failures. No merge or release has been performed.
